{"He keeps smiling all the time, smiling like a rosy little bedbug that has had its fill. “It was \003nine o’clock\004,” he says once again, “when I called you up, wasn’t it?” I nod my head wearily. Yes, it was nine o’clock. He is certain now that it was nine o’clock because he remembers having taken out his watch.","Tropic of Cancer","Henry Miller",true},
